# {{ repo_name }}

A Python project with this command model:

- `uv` manages environments and dependencies.
- `task <namespace>:<name>` runs developer workflows and setup commands.

## Requirements
- Python {{ python_version }}+
- `uv`
- Go Task v3 as a standalone executable (validated with 3.53.1)

Install Task with `brew install go-task` on macOS or `winget install Task.Task` on Windows.
For Linux and other installation methods, see the [native installation instructions](https://taskfile.dev/docs/installation).
Install `uv` using its [installation instructions](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/).
Confirm both executables are on PATH with `task --version` and `uv --version`.

## Initialize The Repo
```bash
task repo:init
task quality:verify
```

`task repo:init` syncs dependencies, installs the Git hooks, and links the optional
[shared agent docs](docs/evergreen/runbook.md#shared-agent-docs) when `~/agent-docs` exists.

## Run
```bash
task app:run
```

## Commands
`task help` lists the available workflows. The [runbook](docs/evergreen/runbook.md) has the
command model, the task namespaces, dependency management, and secret scanning.

